«
@@ ============================================================
@@ TAS3GS — true airspeed and wind from three GPS ground speeds.
@@
@@ Fly three legs at the same indicated airspeed and altitude, on
@@ headings 120° apart, and note the ground speed of each.
@@ Input:  H1 GS1 GS2 GS3 — the first heading (degrees if a plain
@@         number), and the ground speeds on H1, H1+120° and H1+240°
@@         (knots if plain numbers).
@@ Output: the true airspeed TAS, the direction the wind comes from WD
@@         and its speed WS, tagged.
@@ Method: Ed Williams, Aviation Formulary, "Determining the TAS and
@@ the wind from three GPS ground speeds"; the wind direction then
@@ follows from the ground speeds along each heading.
@@ Angle mode and angle units setting are restored before returning.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@ ============================================================

  'AngleMode' RCL 'SetAngleUnits' RCL
  RAD NoAngleUnits
  → hd1 gv1 gv2 gv3 amode aunits
  «
    hd1 IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_° CONVERT UVAL END
    gv1 IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_knot CONVERT UVAL END
    gv2 IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_knot CONVERT UVAL END
    gv3 IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_knot CONVERT UVAL END
    → h g1 g2 g3
    «
      g1 SQ g2 SQ + g3 SQ + 3 /
      → vms
      «
        g1 SQ vms / 1 -  g2 SQ vms / 1 -  g3 SQ vms / 1 -
        → ea eb ec
        «
          ea SQ eb SQ + ec SQ + 6 /
          → mq
          «
            IF mq 0.25 > THEN
              "TAS3GS: inconsistent ground speeds" DOERR
            END
            0.5 0.25 mq - √ +
            → bp
            «
              vms bp * √  vms mq * bp / √
              → tv wv
              «
                0 0
                { } g1 + g2 + g3 +
                → gl
                «
                  0 2 FOR kk
                    gl kk 1 + GET SQ tv SQ - wv SQ - 2 tv * /
                    h 120 kk * + Ⓒπ →Num * 180 /
                    → pp hk
                    «
                      pp hk SIN * 2 * 3 / +
                      SWAP pp hk COS * 2 * 3 / + SWAP
                    »
                  NEXT
                »
                → wn we
                «
                  tv 1_knot * "TAS" →TAG
                  '(-we)∠(-wn)' EVAL 180 * Ⓒπ →Num / 360 + 360 MOD
                  1_° * "WD" →TAG
                  wv 1_knot * "WS" →TAG
                »
              »
            »
          »
        »
      »
    »
    amode EVAL IF aunits THEN SetAngleUnits ELSE NoAngleUnits END
  »
»
